2c. Commends the significant contribution made by the Committee on Petitions, through its work, to the adoption of the new Environmental Crime Directive1a, which seeks to help achieve the objectives of the European Green Deal by providing a comprehensive and up-to-date list of environmental offences and by fighting, by means of criminal law, the most serious breaches of environmental obligations, which could have devastating effects on both the environment and human health;

---

1a Directive (EU) 2024/1203 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 11 April 2024 on the protection of the environment through criminal law and replacing Directives 2008/99/EC and 2009/123/EC OJ L, 2024/1203, 30.4.2024, ELI: [http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2024/1203/oj](http://data.europa.eu/eli/dir/2024/1203/oj)).
